---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CtaRow from "../components/CtaRow.astro";
import FaqBlock from "../components/FaqBlock.astro";
import ProofBar from "../components/ProofBar.astro";
import LeadForm from "@coriolis/lead-form/LeadForm.astro";
import { FAQ_HOME_BASED } from "../lib/faq";
import { PATHS, linkClass, planAnchor } from "../lib/links";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
import { withBase } from "../lib/base";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="FFL Software for a Home-Based Business | FFL Accelerator"
  description="FFL software for a home based business: records software, a website, and a register only if you sell in person. Small business FFL software, explained."
  path="/ffl-software-home-based-business/"
  faq={FAQ_HOME_BASED}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 lg:py-24">
    <h1 class="type-display text-5xl sm:text-6xl">
      FFL software for a home-based business
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      A home-based FFL usually needs two pieces of software: records software
      and a website. A register only matters if you also sell in person. FFL
      Accelerator is the website.
    </p>
    <ProofBar />

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <h2 class="type-display text-3xl">The software a home-based FFL needs</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        Small business FFL software doesn't have to be one big system. It's
        three separate jobs, and a home-based shop may only need two of them.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Records.</strong> Records software keeps the bound book and the
        paperwork your license depends on. That job belongs to a dedicated
        records vendor and your counsel. It is not us, and nothing on this site
        is legal advice.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        <strong>The register.</strong> Optional. If you don't sell at a counter,
        you may not need one.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        <strong>The website.</strong> Your public store, on your own domain, and
        you own it. This is the job FFL Accelerator does.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        See <a href={withBase(PATHS.guide)} class={linkClass}>which FFL software does which job</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <h2 class="type-display text-3xl">Selling without a storefront or stock</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        Dropshipping can run without a retail floor. You still need a valid FFL.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        FFL Accelerator connects <a href={planAnchor("inventory-dropshipping")} class={linkClass}>distributor catalogs</a>, keeps inventory updated, and handles automated dropshipping. Sell your own stock, the catalogs, or both.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        FFL Checkout handles the FFL step at checkout. Your records system stays
        your records system.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        Rules for running from home depend on where you are. Ask your attorney
        before you set up. This is not legal advice.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <h2 class="type-display text-3xl">If you also sell in person</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        Keep the register you already run. FFL Accelerator connects your
        existing register when you want the counter and the site to share
        inventory, and any register that works with WooCommerce can connect.
        When it's connected, the register and the website sync both ways.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-line pt-8">
      <h2 class="type-display text-3xl">What the website includes</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        Hosting, design, FFL Checkout, distributor catalogs, email campaigns and
        analytics, with a webmaster included. Pick a setup: Basic Setup, a
        Branded Online Storefront, or Retail Setup, a Full Custom Website. Then
        one monthly plan. Month to month. MSA at signup.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        See <a href={withBase(PATHS.plan)} class={linkClass}>what's included</a>, and how we handle <a href={withBase(PATHS.hosting)} class={linkClass}>hosting and upkeep</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        Already selling online? We can <a href={withBase(PATHS.migration)} class={linkClass}>move your current site</a> without taking it offline.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>

  <FaqBlock items={FAQ_HOME_BASED} title="Questions from home-based FFLs" />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 lg:py-24">
    <h2 class="type-display text-3xl">Tell us how you sell today</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      Online only, by appointment, or at a counter. Tell us how you work and
      we'll show you where the website fits. Rather talk? Call <a href={SITE.phoneHref} class={linkClass}>{SITE.phone}</a>.
    </p>
    <div class="relative mt-8 bg-paper-2 p-6 sm:p-8">
      <LeadForm site="fflaccelerator" defaultPillar="Ecommerce" pillars={["Ecommerce"]} />
    </div>
    <CtaRow />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
